cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these notebooks, please cite them as below and name the notebook you used."
title: "ganymede: open HPC notebooks from Eugo"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Eugo, Inc."
    website: "https://eugo.io"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebooks for high-performance and scientific Python: case studies on public NOAA and
  Copernicus data (GOES-16 land surface temperature, National Water Model streamflow forecasts,
  Sentinel-2 resampling), Ray patterns for parallel and distributed computing (Ray Core, Data,
  Serve, Train and Tune), demos of popular data, geospatial and visualisation libraries, and smoke
  tests for Python packages and native libraries.
repository-code: "https://github.com/eugo-inc/ganymede"
url: "https://eugo-inc.github.io/ganymede/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
